  "body": "Stacked on #2992. Review the [changes above the #2992 head](https://github.com/qsmits/Camcraft/compare/db8a61aba...fa31e7120).\n\n## What changed\n\nA Wire Contour punch can now use one selected closed DXF chain that is a convex loop of tangent lines and arcs. Before, only a circle or a racetrack was possible (#2022). The native wire EDM job keeps each nominal line end and each arc centre.\n\nThe port puts the work of #2993 on the current frame:\n\n- Geometry (`camcraft-geometry`): `wire_round_profile::WireProfile` holds a `RoundProfile` (circle or racetrack, #2022) or a new `TangentProfile`. `WireProfile::from_chain` reads a circle or a racetrack first, so `CIRCLE20` and `RACE20` do not change. Every other chain must pass the tangent proof: tangent joints, counter-clockwise arcs of at most 180 degrees, arc turns that total one revolution, radii from 0.5 to 20 mm, at most 128 segments. The preview polygon encloses each arc within 0.000025 mm and is checked against the analytic support of the loop (at most 2,048 vertices).\n- App (`camcraft-app`): `SelectedWireChain::wire_profile` replaces `round_profile`. `agie_sketch_job` returns the `WireProfile` and checks the rest of the drawing against the exact bounds of the loop plus the 0.4 mm rough and wire margin.\n- Post (`camcraft-post`): the new `agie/tangent_profile.rs` gives the same `ArcBlock` list and `PunchSetup20` as `round_profile.rs` (#2978). Each joint and centre must be on the five-decimal grid within 1e-9 mm. No value is rounded. The post checks the exact squared radius at both arc ends and the tangent direction at each joint in integer grid units. The entry is perpendicular to a straight side parallel to X or Y, from the waste side, with 3 mm of straight on each side of the seam. The stock must have 0.4 mm beyond the exact bounds of the loop. The quality is CCB030 through `contour::punch_setup`, with no own quality object (#2984). `export_round_with_review` now takes a `&WireProfile`.\n- The old writer file of the PR (`tangent_profile.rs` on the deleted `Work`) and its new top-level test binary `agie_dxf.rs` are not used.\n\n## Readings on the emulated control\n\nWe imported `ROUND20` and `THREEARC` on an offline copy of the Classic Cut 2S control. No physical cut was made.\n\n- Both jobs: the ISO and SBL bytes on the control disk agree with the source. The work shows `CCB030[0]` after import. FORMALCHECK shows one error, `Technologie : te definiëren`. The quality page shows CCB030, Ra 0.30, Tkm 1.0, Te 1.5. The TECCUT header shows Dia 0.25, H 20, Ra 0.30, Tkm 1.0, Te 1.5, row 0199. After `Toewijzen` the work shows `CCB030[4]` with the offsets 245, 155, 140 and 134 µm. FORMALCHECK then gives `geen fouten`. The only warnings are `Uitgekozen opties : 131072` and `Referentiewaarden : te definiëren`.\n- `ROUND20`: the J00 keeps the four arc centres (14, −8), (16, 10), (−14, 8) and (−16, −10) on every pass. The rough radii are 6.245 and 4.245 mm, then 6.155/4.155, 6.140/4.140 and 6.134/4.134 mm. The separation is from X0 to X−1: 1.000 mm.\n- `THREEARC`: the J00 keeps the centres (24, 0), (0, 18) and (0, 0) on every pass. The oblique side moves along its normal by each offset. The separation is from X12 to X11: 1.000 mm.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `camcraft-app` `agie_native` (module `tangent`): `a_mixed_radius_loop_posts_each_nominal_arc_and_the_checked_setup`, `an_oblique_tangent_side_joins_three_distinct_arcs` (goldens `ROUND20.ISO` and `THREEARC.ISO`; the SBL is the checked `CCSEP20` setup with only the stem and the hole changed), `a_short_inner_offgrid_edge_or_folded_loop_publishes_nothing`.\n- `camcraft-post` lib (`agie::tangent_profile_tests`): the ISO of both loops, and the refusals for a short or inner entry, an off-grid joint, a thin stock margin, a die and a 40 mm plate.\n- `camcraft-geometry` lib (`wire_round_profile::tests`, `wire_round_profile::tangent::tests`): the tangent proof, the bounds, the preview, and the refusals for a folded loop, a corner and a circle radius.\n- `camcraft-app` `agie_native` (module `quality`): `ra035_refuses_a_group_an_arc_punch_a_die_and_a_cutoff` now also refuses the Ra 0.35 request on the tangent `rounded-punch` example. No control data covers CCB035 on an arc punch.\n- The existing goldens `CIRCLE20`, `RACE20` and `CCSEP20` do not change.\n\nGoldens added: `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/agie-native/ROUND20.ISO` and `THREEARC.ISO`. The other golden differences against main belong to the parent #2992. No golden that is on main changes.\n\nScreenshots: no UI change.\n\n## Gate\n\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` on `fa31e7120`: 1,201 steps in 50 minutes, 0 failed, 0 stalled. Strict Clippy (`-D warnings`, all targets) passed for `camcraft-post`, `camcraft-geometry`, `camcraft-app` and `camcraft-ui`. No heavy lane ran (P6). The ISO bytes of `ROUND20` and `THREEARC` are the same as the bytes that the control read.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- An entry on an oblique straight or on an arc. The post refuses it.\n- A die opening with tangent arcs. The post refuses it.\n- A physical cut.\n\nChangelog: A Wire Contour punch can use a convex DXF loop of tangent lines and arcs. The native wire EDM job keeps each nominal line and arc, including unequal corner radii and oblique sides.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nRefs #2022\nFixes #2983\n",
